test-make-wiring gate: red-first evidence, 2026-08-30
Each assertion proven by its own red; gate/Makefile restored and
re-run green between every red (git diff clean of fixtures).

=== Red 1: collision check (one target in two classes) ===
Fixture: test-network added to GRANDFATHERED while already in BROKEN.
Output:
  FAIL: a target appears in more than one exemption class
  exit=1
Refused with the collision message itself, not a downstream
membership error.  Fixture removed; green confirmed.

=== Folding proof (continuation branch) ===
Baseline, unwrapped test: line:
  test-make-wiring: 16 wired, 3 exempt, 4 grandfathered (review owed), 1 broken (repair owed); 24 test-* targets, 17 deps on `test:`

Fixture: test: wrapped across two lines with a trailing backslash
(space-indented continuation).  make -n test exit=0, so the fixture
is a Makefile make itself accepts.

FIRST folded run -- the branch was BROKEN:
  test-make-wiring: 7 wired, ...; 24 test-* targets, 9 deps on `test:`
  gate-exit=1
Cause: the inline regex ^test:(.*(?:\\\n.*)*)$ succeeds greedily on
the first physical line alone -- the continuation group legally
matches zero times, multiline $ accepts the spot, and a successful
match is never backtracked into.  The .replace('\\\n', ' ') after
the search was folding a capture that never held a continuation.

Fix: fold continuations across the whole source BEFORE the search
(src.replace('\\\n', ' ')), regex reduced to ^test:(.*)$.

Folded run after fix:
  test-make-wiring: 16 wired, ...; 24 test-* targets, 17 deps on `test:`
  gate-exit=0
Unwrapped, re-run:
  test-make-wiring: 16 wired, ...; 24 test-* targets, 17 deps on `test:`
  gate-exit=0
9 vs 17 was the signal; identical 17/16 folded and unwrapped is the
proof.

=== Red A: orphaned suite (wired target removed from test:) ===
Fixture: test-survey deleted from the test: dependency line.
Output:
  FAIL: test-survey wired or exempt -- orphaned suite -- wire it into `test:` or exempt it WITH a true reason
  Passed: 32/33
  exit=1
Names that target only.  Restored; green.

=== Red B: empty exemption reason ===
Fixture: GRANDFATHERED['test-cortexm'] reason set to ''.
Output:
  FAIL: test-cortexm grandfathered with reason -- empty reason -- an exemption without a reason is an orphan with paperwork
  Passed: 32/33
  exit=1
Restored; green.

=== Red C: exemption entry for a target that IS wired ===
Fixture: test-survey (wired) added to GRANDFATHERED with a
RED-ONLY reason.
Output:
  FAIL: grandfathered entry test-survey still unwired -- target is wired now -- the entry is stale, delete it (for BROKEN entries: the repair that wired it must also remove the entry, not leave a lie about a suite that now works)
  Passed: 33/34
  exit=1
Staleness fires; the entry cannot accumulate as a lie.  Restored.

